cards.body:
ICE (I2 violation): looping over a list of non-clonable elements makes codegen emit .cloned()/.clone() on the element type; JetTask implements no Clone, so rustc rejects the generated Rust and the compiler exits 101. Owner ruling in chat (2026-07-30): 'Ok we must fix this issue.'

Repro:
  use core.tasks as tasks
  fn run() {
      handles :: [tasks.spawn(() => 1), tasks.spawn(() => 2)]
      loop t; handles { t.wait() }
  }
jet run --release → internal compiler error, rustc E0277 JetTask<()>: Clone.

Direction: sema/TIR loop lowering must not insert implicit clones for non-Copy/non-Clone element types. A loop over such a list should borrow (if the body only borrows) or consume the list with move-out iteration (t.wait() consumes the handle — same semantics tasks.join_all already has). If neither is provable, emit a real sema diagnostic (registered code + UI snapshot, I4) instead of reaching rustc.

Acceptance: repro runs on AOT, jet run, and interpreter with identical output (I9); an example under examples/features/concurrency or memory with golden; no jit_gaps entry; existing loop goldens stay green. Related: #1323 (*_all helpers) reduces how often users write this loop but does not replace the fix.

